WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:01.410
- It's kind of like betting,

00:00:01.410 --> 00:00:05.465
like I see your conspiracy
theory and I raise you aliens.

00:00:05.465 --> 00:00:08.215
(suspense music)

00:00:10.740 --> 00:00:14.913
- My mom sends me articles
about conspiracy stories

00:00:14.913 --> 00:00:19.913
on WeChat, one of the most
memorable ones is about flu shot.

00:00:21.490 --> 00:00:24.900
So according to this conspiracy story,

00:00:24.900 --> 00:00:28.800
all the flu shot are
actually made by aliens.

00:00:28.800 --> 00:00:33.800
Apparently, aliens and American
government have made a deal.

00:00:34.130 --> 00:00:38.650
Aliens wanted to slowly
change human race to aliens

00:00:38.650 --> 00:00:41.880
by injecting flu shot,
at least once a year

00:00:41.880 --> 00:00:43.320
just like iPhone upgrade.

00:00:43.320 --> 00:00:45.530
- The most memorable
WhatsApp conspiracy theory

00:00:45.530 --> 00:00:47.660
that my mom sent me was this picture,

00:00:47.660 --> 00:00:49.155
and it was so graphic it was like

00:00:49.155 --> 00:00:52.730
a blown up hand next to a phone.

00:00:52.730 --> 00:00:55.350
And I'm like, "Mom, why
are you sending me this?"

00:00:55.350 --> 00:00:58.590
Underneath it it's like this
big long paragraph about

00:00:58.590 --> 00:01:01.200
how talking to your phone is really bad

00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:05.180
and like it also has a
high chance of exploding

00:01:05.180 --> 00:01:08.500
and so under that my mom
puts, "Salem, please,

00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:11.610
don't put your phone up
to your face anymore.

00:01:11.610 --> 00:01:12.443
It's bad."

00:01:12.443 --> 00:01:14.710
It's like when you get these
messages from your parents,

00:01:14.710 --> 00:01:15.856
just say, "Okay."

00:01:15.856 --> 00:01:16.760
(laughs)

00:01:16.760 --> 00:01:18.140
Don't debate them on it.

00:01:18.140 --> 00:01:20.660
Don't say anything just say, "Okay."

00:01:20.660 --> 00:01:21.610
And move on.

00:01:21.610 --> 00:01:23.770
- So this one, I don't even
have the contact saved,

00:01:23.770 --> 00:01:25.305
so it just says a phone number.

00:01:25.305 --> 00:01:29.138
(reading in foreign language)

00:01:30.918 --> 00:01:33.552
(sped up speaking in foreign language)

00:01:33.552 --> 00:01:36.750
(jazz music)

00:01:36.750 --> 00:01:38.560
Essentially, what this long-ass message

00:01:38.560 --> 00:01:39.730
is trying to say

00:01:39.730 --> 00:01:42.077
is that secret Chinese operatives

00:01:42.077 --> 00:01:46.049
have created highly advanced technology

00:01:46.049 --> 00:01:49.012
that can hide phishing information

00:01:49.012 --> 00:01:52.000
in "good morning" pictures,

00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:54.897
"good night" gifs, and cute little videos.

00:01:54.897 --> 00:01:57.710
So you should not be sending
your friends and family

00:01:57.710 --> 00:02:00.220
cat pictures or dog videos,

00:02:00.220 --> 00:02:02.630
'cause your credit card
PIN will get stolen.

00:02:02.630 --> 00:02:05.980
- So I use Facebook Messenger and WhatsApp

00:02:05.980 --> 00:02:08.420
to communicate with my mom.

00:02:08.420 --> 00:02:10.500
She will send me articles, videos,

00:02:10.500 --> 00:02:12.240
and everything in between.

00:02:12.240 --> 00:02:14.900
She automatically sends me, you know,

00:02:14.900 --> 00:02:18.230
articles that if I am
walking around barefoot,

00:02:18.230 --> 00:02:19.660
I am gonna get sick,

00:02:19.660 --> 00:02:23.980
or if I sit on the hot concrete,

00:02:23.980 --> 00:02:25.565
I'm gonna get a UTI.

00:02:25.565 --> 00:02:26.398
(laughs)

00:02:26.398 --> 00:02:29.310
- So, my uncle, all he does
is kind of like surf the web,

00:02:29.310 --> 00:02:31.530
and I think he's in the deep web for sure,

00:02:31.530 --> 00:02:35.145
'cause he finds weird-ass
videos and sends them to us.

00:02:35.145 --> 00:02:38.650
So, like, he sent my entire family,

00:02:38.650 --> 00:02:40.090
every person in my family,

00:02:40.090 --> 00:02:42.600
and probably other people
outside our family,

00:02:42.600 --> 00:02:45.330
this video that claims chicken meat,

00:02:45.330 --> 00:02:48.426
that we eat, is actually rat meat,

00:02:48.426 --> 00:02:52.130
and it got so bad that, you know,

00:02:52.130 --> 00:02:55.285
months and weeks have passed,
and on multiple occasions,

00:02:55.285 --> 00:02:59.830
my dad at family gatherings
will bring up this source,

00:02:59.830 --> 00:03:02.710
and be like, "Yeah, I heard, you know,

00:03:02.710 --> 00:03:04.990
the chicken we're eating is actually rat."

00:03:04.990 --> 00:03:06.810
This is wrong information.

00:03:06.810 --> 00:03:09.370
When he sends me anything
I still need to respond.

00:03:09.370 --> 00:03:11.090
Like, I feel bad, I'm not gonna not reply.

00:03:11.090 --> 00:03:14.160
It's his daily, probably,
routine, it's part of his day.

00:03:14.160 --> 00:03:17.871
- Because my parents don't trust me living

00:03:17.871 --> 00:03:21.560
in America by myself,
therefore they send me

00:03:21.560 --> 00:03:25.710
a lot of conspiracy stories
to make me be more cautious.

00:03:25.710 --> 00:03:29.080
- I think she was, she
just wants us to be aware

00:03:29.080 --> 00:03:31.470
of everything, and take care of ourselves.

00:03:31.470 --> 00:03:32.770
- At the end of the day, immigrant parents

00:03:32.770 --> 00:03:34.650
are always just trying to keep us safe,

00:03:34.650 --> 00:03:37.270
so that's why they send
us all this crazy stuff.

00:03:37.270 --> 00:03:39.260
- I think at the heart of
it, it's really this idea

00:03:39.260 --> 00:03:41.620
of like "I care about my family member,

00:03:41.620 --> 00:03:42.880
and I want them to know this."

00:03:42.880 --> 00:03:46.530
And that ranges from a
cute picture of your kid,

00:03:46.530 --> 00:03:48.690
to "Something's happening with the CIA

00:03:48.690 --> 00:03:49.940
and we need to know about it."

00:03:49.940 --> 00:03:51.730
- I think, at the end of the day,

00:03:51.730 --> 00:03:53.750
I might miss them when she does stop

00:03:53.750 --> 00:03:55.620
sending me those articles.

00:03:55.620 --> 00:03:59.340
- I would say, "Keep on
sending 'em, fam, it's great."

